# What is known of a place's things is each member's own; the map and its ways are the party's.
#
# An observation names a thing on the map of a later visit — for the member who looked. A companion
# who did not look still sees an anonymous symbol there, unless they were told: speaking of a thing
# to a companion makes it known to them too. The areas stood in and the ways gone by stay shared.
#
# The protagonist looks at the rack and at the bell and speaks of the bell to the companion. The
# party leaves and comes back: the protagonist's map names both, the companion's names the bell only.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --allow-reentry --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon --organs encephalon=6

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]

click observe "Test Rack"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click observe "Test Bell"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click speak "Test Bell" to Brindletail
choose friendship
advance 12 180
expect-state trees speech

# Each entry is one member's: the rack is the protagonist's alone, the bell is both of theirs.
inspect known
expect-state known Protagonist>poi|
expect-state known Brindletail>poi|

# Out and back in: the trees are gone, and what each member knew is named on their own map.
click exit
wait mode WorldView 120
advance 12 120
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
advance 12 180
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]
inspect symbols
expect-state symbols click observe "Test Rack" in "Test Yard"
expect-state symbols click observe "Test Bell" in "Test Yard"

click member Brindletail
wait
expect [BRINDLETAIL]
inspect symbols
expect-state symbols click observe "Test Bell" in "Test Yard"
expect-no-state symbols click observe "Test Rack"
quit
